# The guide book (1.4.1). Update it along with the README's how-to-play. Keep each page short enough to fit.
weakspot.stats.guide=Guide
weakspot.guide.1.title=Welcome
weakspot.guide.1.text=Glowing circles (weak spots) appear on blocks and creatures. Hit one to dig, grow or work faster, and it moves elsewhere. You can still play as usual without them.
weakspot.guide.2.title=Mining
weakspot.guide.2.text=Hold left click to mine and a weak spot appears on the face. Aim at it while mining to hit it and dig faster. The green bar below it shows the block's remaining health.
weakspot.guide.3.title=Repairs and Milestones
weakspot.guide.3.text=Hitting weak spots while breaking blocks slowly repairs the tool in your hand. Milestones come often, from 50 up to 100000 hits and beyond, with a celebration, XP and repairs. Every other kind of weak spot, and your total of all kinds, has milestones too.
weakspot.guide.4.title=Growing Crops
weakspot.guide.4.text=Hold right click with an empty hand on a growing crop or sapling. Each hit on its weak spot grows it a little. Sugar cane, cactus and nether wart too. The yellow bar shows growth. If it cannot grow (too dark, for example), chat tells you.
weakspot.guide.5.title=Faster Machines
weakspot.guide.5.text=Sneak with both hands empty and hold right click on a machine, such as a furnace. Hit its weak spot and it speeds up right away; its speed shows under the crosshair and grows with your combo. Furnaces, brewing stands and spawners show a progress bar. Comparators work too.
weakspot.guide.6.title=Animals
weakspot.guide.6.text=Hold right click with an empty hand on an animal. Hits speed up growing up, breeding cooldown, wool, eggs and villager trade restocks. Sneak for horses, villagers and the like.
weakspot.guide.7.title=Fishing
weakspot.guide.7.text=While your bobber waits in the water, a weak spot appears around it. Keep the rod in hand, aim at the spot and left click to make fish come sooner.
weakspot.guide.8.title=Bows
weakspot.guide.8.text=While drawing a bow, a weak spot appears a little away from the crosshair. Move your aim onto it to draw faster. Hits after a full draw power up the arrow (up to +50%). The gauge shows the draw.
weakspot.guide.9.title=Melee
weakspot.guide.9.text=Hold a sword or axe near enemies and a silver weak spot appears left or right of your crosshair. Each hit charges up; your next strike on an enemy becomes a critical hit, boosted by the charge. Switching items clears it.
weakspot.guide.10.title=Combos and Sounds
weakspot.guide.10.text=Keep hitting and the hit sound climbs the scale while a combo count shows under the crosshair. It carries across kinds and ends after about 2 seconds without a hit. Big steps up to 1000 are celebrated.
weakspot.guide.11.title=Keys
weakspot.guide.11.text=%s: turn weak spots on or off (handy while building). %s: the stats screen, where you can also change hit sounds, turn each kind of weak spot on or off, pick its color, open the settings and read this guide. Found a bug? Type /weakspot bug.
weakspot.guide.12.title=Multiplayer
weakspot.guide.12.text=Weak spots that nearby friends are hitting show as rings in another color, and you hear their hits too. Combos over 10 show above their heads. Colors, shapes and volume can be changed in the settings.
weakspot.guide.13.title=Vehicles
weakspot.guide.13.text=Riding a horse, pig, minecart or boat, a weak spot appears near the crosshair (straight above or below on horses and pigs). Aim at it to speed up; combos make it faster. Bow hits while riding keep the speed.
weakspot.guide.14.title=Eating
weakspot.guide.14.text=While eating or drinking, a green weak spot appears a little away from the crosshair. Aim at it to finish sooner: two hits and you are done.
weakspot.guide.15.title=Sleeping
weakspot.guide.15.text=Sleeping in a bed at night shows a marker on the sleep screen. Click it to move time forward and bring the morning sooner. Time is shared by everyone.
